---
import footage from '~/assets/footage/linesweeper.mp4?url';
import poster from '~/assets/captures/linesweeper-play.png';
---

<figure class="capture footage">
	<video
		controls
		playsinline
		preload="none"
		poster={poster.src}
		width="1280"
		height="720"
		aria-label="LineSweeper gameplay"
		aria-describedby="linesweeper-footage-description"
	>
		<source src={footage} type="video/mp4" />
		Your browser cannot play this video. Use the download link below to watch it.
	</video>
	<figcaption>
		A complete scripted match. 35 seconds, no sound.{' '}
		<a href={footage} download="linesweeper.mp4">Download the MP4</a>.
	</figcaption>
	<details class="footage-description">
		<summary>Read a description of the video</summary>
		<p id="linesweeper-footage-description">
			Coloured pieces turn and slide into a falling-block well. Completed rows disappear,
			throwing matching sparks sideways as the score and line count rise. The hold slot keeps
			one piece in reserve, and the next five pieces appear beside the board. Later the stack
			reaches the top: a “TOPPED OUT” banner appears and thousands of coloured particles burst
			across the screen, then fade. The game has no sound or spoken commentary.
		</p>
	</details>
</figure>
